Read [Poteto mode for Pi](../SKILL.md) and [the plan contract](../../../docs/templates/pstack-plan.md) before acting. Resolve skill names through `read <package>/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` or `/skill:<name>`; load them on demand. `/unslop` replaces Cursor's deslop pass. Use Pi's `read`, `edit`, `write`, `ffgrep`/`grep`, `fffind`/`find`, and `ls` for file content; `bash` executes programs and checks. Ask the operator in plain text when a real decision or blocker requires human input.

- **Subagents (`Task` replacement).** Spawn workers and sub-coordinators through pi-subagents' `subagent` tool using registered `pstack.*` agents (`pstack.poteto-agent` on the configured `code` role for PR owners and implementation workers, `pstack.verifier` on `verification` or `pstack.comment-sicko` on `review` for independent verifiers). Fan out independent workers in one parallel call: `subagent({ workflow: "parallel", args: { tasks: [{ agent: "pstack.poteto-agent", task: "<kickoff and exclusive worktree path>" }] } })`. Configure role models and thinking levels with `/setup-pstack`; never put `model` on the outer `subagent` call or inside a parallel task item. Wait for native completion notices; never poll or message an idle subagent to check on it. When new work needs a worker's built checkout, uncommitted changes, or running process, resume or follow up on that worker; otherwise start a fresh worker with consolidated context. If `pi-subagents` is unavailable or delegation is forbidden by the operator, stay within the current grant, label self-review, and report `BLOCKED: independent review`.
- **Local worktrees (no cloud VM).** Upstream runs workers on a new cloud VM (`environment: "cloud"`), which Pi does not provide. Start each independent worker in an isolated local git worktree (`subagent({ agent: "pstack.poteto-agent", task: "<kickoff>", cwd: "<source-repo>", worktree: true })` from a clean checkout, or pre-create a worktree with `git worktree add <path> -b <branch> HEAD` and pass `cwd: "<path>", worktree: false`). Keep one writer per worktree and branch; a replacement worker takes over only after the previous writer has stopped. Work that must use this machine directly (a `control-ui` or `control-cli` runtime check through the operator's available browser or CLI driver, reading local Pi session transcripts, a local simulator, or auth that exists only on this machine) runs locally within the scoped paths named in its kickoff.
- **Project tracker and Project store.** Keep the Project tracker (`<run-id>/orchestrate/notes.md`), kickoffs, verdicts, and local trails under `<run-id>/orchestrate/` in the pstack run directory provided in the system prompt, or another durable operator-approved local directory; never inside the target repository unless authorized and never at a hard-coded home path. Keep one writer per file: the coordinator writes shared program state and `notes.md`, while workers return their reports and never edit shared store files.
- **PR and CI watching (no `orch` CLI or polling scripts).** Use host PR and CI event subscriptions when the harness provides them. When the host does not provide event subscriptions, follow [the Babysit playbook](babysit.md) and pstack's bounded `/loop` practice: take read-only PR snapshots with `node "<package-root>/scripts/watch-pr.mjs" --repo "<repo-path>" --pr <number> --status-only --pretty` (or `--green` as a `/loop run --until` predicate) on GitHub, or `origin pr view <pr> --checks --comments` and `origin pr checks <pr> --watch` on Origin. Call no `orch` CLI, write no custom polling loops, and never add a second sleep loop.

A concrete bounded `/loop` cadence when driving a plan contract in TUI or RPC mode (replace the package, repository, and plan paths first):

```text
/loop run --max-turns 8 --until "cd '/absolute/target-repository' && node '/absolute/pi-pstack/scripts/check-plan.mjs' --complete '/absolute/run/<run-id>/orchestrate/plan.md'" "Read notes.md and the plan; check live PR state and current-head verdicts, advance only authorized units, and update the Project tracker and store. Stop on a hold or exhausted budget."
```

- **Forge and authority gates.** Resolve the forge once: GitHub CLI (`gh pr view`, `gh pr checks`) is the default; when `command -v origin` succeeds and resolves the repository, use `origin pr view <pr> --checks --comments` and `origin pr checks <pr>` as the forge equivalents. Never require Graphite (`gt`). Pushing, opening, editing, retargeting, or closing a PR, rebasing, force-pushing, and merging each require explicit authorization in the current session for the action and scope; auto-merge requires its own explicit grant. Without push/PR or merge authorization, prepare commits, PR bodies, and current-head verdicts locally and report the pending gate.
